version: 2.0.0
description: >-
  The Paradigm Claude Code plugin (`paradigm@a-paradigm` marketplace install).
  It wires the MCP server, the enforcement hooks, the agents and the skills into
  every project. Users install it; nothing here is built at runtime.
components:
  claude-code-plugin:
    description: >-
      Plugin layout. .claude-plugin/plugin.json is the manifest (name, version
      kept in step with @a-company/paradigm, keywords). hooks/hooks.json maps
      Claude Code hook events to the scripts. scripts/*.sh are the hook scripts
      (scripts/paradigm-common.sh, scripts/paradigm-stop.sh and the rest),
      COPIES generated from packages/paradigm/src/commands/hooks/scripts by
      packages/paradigm/scripts/generate-hooks.mjs; edit the sources there and
      run `node scripts/generate-hooks.mjs` (`--check` must be clean).
      scripts/migrate-to-plugin.sh moves a pre-plugin install onto the plugin.
      agents/*.md are the bundled subagent definitions and skills/ the bundled
      skills. README.md is the user-facing install guide.
    type: config
    files:
      - .claude-plugin/plugin.json
      - hooks/hooks.json
      - scripts/paradigm-common.sh
      - scripts/migrate-to-plugin.sh
    components:
      - '#paradigm-hooks'
    tags: [plugin, claude-code, hooks]
